  "body": "## Scope \u2014 dependent stage, not a second port\n\nStage #271 after #295, before multithreading tuning. This reuses John's `candidate/sam-271-on-next` (`de9585b24e0b45cad822de80ee51bcb576911cc3`): his supplied five-commit series is applied on the settled distinct-index foundation. The only textual conflict was the finalize_each doc line; both distinct-index and staged-prefix documentation are retained. No new API type, Hasher field, worker count or threshold.\n\nThe first-chunk gather avoids serial prefix compression and unnecessary turn allocations, retaining bytes in the existing chunk buffer/stage. The current consuming API resets both the ready and staged fast paths after completion.\n\nKernel, generator and theorem bytes match frozen #271 `7c4166fa922165c7db8250908f6442cb3b9a28a2`; frozen review heads remain unchanged. John's rebased native/ARM/proof/generator checks are prior evidence, not newly attributed results.\n\n**Draft: fresh exact-source x86/native and grouped-update complete-cycle checks are being prepared.** The intended direct baseline is #295's exact tested integration tree `d4f675f4967317b41546e8c8309d35eb384cbbaf`, not the pre-foundation API. New whole-cycle data will include descriptor refill, grouped updates, digest production and reset; the individual-update probe does not establish this optimization's gain.\n\nFinish-only/sparse-use costs remain beside the complete-work gain in assigned #270. John explicitly judged that trade acceptable for the original mechanism; new source-specific costs will be recorded rather than assumed equal. No composite ratios or global Pareto claim.\n\nIntegration order remains #295 then this stage. No organization merge/release/tag/upload performed by Sam.\n\n\u2014 Sam Shackleton\n",
